title: The Front responds to Hazhir's assassination
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1949 and month >= 11 and hazhir_seen = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 30
on-arrival: hazhir_seen = 1

= November 1949

Abdolhossein Hazhir is assassinated. The Front must respond to political
violence without claiming responsibility it does not possess.

- @hazhir_condemn: Condemn the killing and insist on constitutional methods
- @hazhir_bounded: Condemn the killing while documenting the wider crisis

@hazhir_condemn
on-arrival: constitutional_legitimacy += 4; religious_network_relation -= 1; shah_relation += 1
go-to: post_event

@hazhir_bounded
on-arrival: constitutional_legitimacy += 2; political_intelligence += 3; religious_network_dissent -= 1
go-to: post_event

@tehran_rerun
title: Tehran's election is cancelled
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1950 and month >= 1 and tehran_rerun_seen = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 10
on-arrival: tehran_rerun_seen = 1; parliamentary_deck_unlocked = 1; majles_phase = "Tehran rerun and disputed returns"

= January 1950

The Tehran election is cancelled and must be rerun. The Front can concentrate
on a defensible slate or extend its monitoring network.

- @rerun_slate: Concentrate resources on a common Tehran slate
- @rerun_monitor: Build the strongest possible record of the rerun

@rerun_slate
on-arrival: election_strategy = "Concentrated Tehran slate"; independent_nationalists_organization += 4; iran_party_relation += 2; public_mandate += 2
go-to: post_event

@rerun_monitor
on-arrival: election_strategy = "Monitoring and credential record"; political_intelligence += 4; parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 3; organizational_reach += 2
go-to: post_event

@chambers_open
title: The Sixteenth Majles and First Senate open
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1950 and month >= 2 and chambers_open_seen = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 10
on-arrival: {!
Q.chambers_open_seen = 1;
Q.majles_convened = 1;
Q.senate_convened = 1;
Q.majles_phase = "Credentials under review";
var vacantIndexes = [0, 87, 107, 126, 128];
var nfIndexes = [38, 39, 40, 41, 42, 44, 45, 105];
for (var i = 0; i < 136; i += 1) {
    if (vacantIndexes.indexOf(i) < 0) Q.majles_places[i].scenario.current_return = "returned";
}
var openingCredentials = 0;
for (var c = 0; c < 136 && openingCredentials < 98; c += 1) {
    if (vacantIndexes.indexOf(c) < 0 && nfIndexes.indexOf(c) < 0) {
        Q.majles_places[c].scenario.credential = "approved";
        Q.majles_places[c].scenario.usability = "usable";
        openingCredentials += 1;
    }
}
for (var n of nfIndexes) {
    Q.majles_places[n].scenario.support = "national_front";
}
for (var s = 0; s < 60; s += 1) {
    Q.senate_places[s].scenario.current_return = "returned";
    Q.senate_places[s].scenario.credential = "approved";
    Q.senate_places[s].scenario.usability = "usable";
}
!}

= February 1950

The two chambers open with different routes to membership. Returns,
credentials, usable membership, alignments, and attendance remain separate in
the campaign ledger.

- @opening_procedure: Make credential procedure the immediate priority
- @opening_coalition: Keep the parliamentary group politically coordinated

@opening_procedure
on-arrival: credentials_strategy = "Case-by-case procedural challenge"; parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 4
go-to: post_event

@opening_coalition
on-arrival: credentials_strategy = "Coordinated National Front group"; independent_nationalists_relation += 3; oil_coalition_support += 2
go-to: post_event

@credential_campaign
title: The credential campaign
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1950 and month >= 5 and credentials_seen = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 10
on-arrival: {!
Q.credentials_seen = 1;
var nfIndexes = [38, 39, 40, 41, 42, 44, 45, 105];
for (var n of nfIndexes) {
    Q.majles_places[n].scenario.current_return = "returned";
    Q.majles_places[n].scenario.credential = "approved";
    Q.majles_places[n].scenario.usability = "usable";
    Q.majles_places[n].scenario.support = "national_front";
}
var approvedCount = 0;
for (var place of Q.majles_places) {
    if (place.scenario.credential === "approved") approvedCount += 1;
}
for (var c = 0; c < 136 && approvedCount < 120; c += 1) {
    if (Q.majles_places[c].scenario.current_return === "returned" &&
        Q.majles_places[c].scenario.credential !== "approved") {
        Q.majles_places[c].scenario.credential = "approved";
        Q.majles_places[c].scenario.usability = "usable";
        approvedCount += 1;
    }
}
!}

= May–June 1950

Credential decisions arrive in waves rather than as a single national result.
The Front's usable parliamentary group takes shape within that process.

- @credentials_public: Publish the strongest documented cases
- @credentials_internal: Preserve relationships needed for later votes

@credentials_public
on-arrival: parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 5; press_capacity += 2; shah_electoral_influence -= 2
go-to: post_event

@credentials_internal
on-arrival: oil_coalition_support += 4; independent_nationalists_relation += 2; political_intelligence += 2
go-to: post_event

@oil_committee_formation
title: The oil committee
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1950 and month >= 5 and majles_convened = 1 and oil_committee_formed = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 20
on-arrival: oil_committee_formed = 1

= May 1950

The Majles creates a committee to consider the supplemental oil agreement.
The Front can insist on term-by-term scrutiny or begin assembling a broader
nationalization coalition.

- @committee_terms: Establish a term-by-term record
- @committee_majority: Build beyond the Front's own deputies

@committee_terms
on-arrival: parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 4; political_intelligence += 3; oil_terms_position = "Documented term-by-term rejection"
go-to: post_event

@committee_majority
on-arrival: oil_coalition_support += 6; independent_nationalists_relation += 2; religious_network_relation += 2
go-to: post_event

@supplemental_campaign
title: The supplemental-agreement campaign
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1950 and month >= 8 and supplemental_campaign_seen = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 10
on-arrival: supplemental_campaign_seen = 1

= August 1950

Debate over the Gass–Golshayan supplemental agreement intensifies. Reports
about other oil arrangements, including the Saudi-Aramco comparison, increase
pressure without making unlike contracts mechanically identical.

- @supplemental_explain: Explain the disputed terms precisely
- @supplemental_mandate: Turn the issue into a public mandate

@supplemental_explain
on-arrival: press_capacity += 4; political_intelligence += 3; constitutional_legitimacy += 2
go-to: post_event

@supplemental_mandate
on-arrival: public_mandate += 5; oil_coalition_support += 3; shah_resistance += 2
go-to: post_event

@committee_rejection
title: The oil committee rejects Gass–Golshayan
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1950 and month >= 12 and gass_golshayan_rejected_committee = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 10
on-arrival: gass_golshayan_rejected_committee = 1

= December 1950

The oil committee rejects the supplemental agreement. The recorded result is
an institutional decision, not a free-floating popularity bonus.

- @committee_claim: Claim the procedural victory narrowly
- @committee_bridge: Use the decision to widen the nationalization coalition

@committee_claim
on-arrival: parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 5; constitutional_legitimacy += 2
go-to: post_event

@committee_bridge
on-arrival: oil_coalition_support += 6; public_mandate += 2
go-to: post_event

@majles_rejection
title: The Majles rejects the supplemental agreement
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1951 and month >= 1 and gass_golshayan_rejected_committee = 1 and gass_golshayan_rejected_majles = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 20
on-arrival: gass_golshayan_rejected_majles = 1

= 11 January 1951

The Majles follows the committee and rejects the supplemental agreement.

- @majles_record: Emphasize the constitutional parliamentary record
- @majles_movement: Emphasize the public coalition behind the vote

@majles_record
on-arrival: parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 4; constitutional_legitimacy += 3
go-to: post_event

@majles_movement
on-arrival: oil_coalition_support += 4; public_mandate += 4; press_capacity += 2
go-to: post_event

@razmara_confrontation
title: Confrontation with Razmara
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1951 and month >= 2 and razmara_confrontation_seen = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 10
on-arrival: razmara_confrontation_seen = 1

= February 1951

Prime Minister Haj Ali Razmara argues against immediate nationalization. The
Front must answer without allowing one disputed exchange to substitute for the
structured oil case.

- @razmara_terms: Answer term by term in parliament
- @razmara_public: Organize a public rebuttal

@razmara_terms
on-arrival: razmara_response = "Parliamentary term-by-term rebuttal"; parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 4; political_intelligence += 2; oil_coalition_support += 3
go-to: post_event

@razmara_public
on-arrival: razmara_response = "Public nationalization campaign"; public_mandate += 5; press_capacity += 3; shah_resistance += 2
go-to: post_event

@razmara_assassination
title: Razmara is assassinated
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1951 and month >= 3 and razmara_assassination_seen = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 10
on-arrival: razmara_assassination_seen = 1

= 7 March 1951

Razmara is assassinated. Responsibility and political consequence must remain
separate: the Front can condemn political killing while continuing its oil
campaign.

- @assassination_condemn: Condemn the killing without qualification
- @assassination_bounded: Condemn it and restate the constitutional oil case

@assassination_condemn
on-arrival: constitutional_legitimacy += 5; religious_network_relation -= 2; shah_relation += 1
go-to: post_event

@assassination_bounded
on-arrival: constitutional_legitimacy += 3; parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 2; oil_coalition_support += 2
go-to: post_event

@nationalization_approval
title: Committee and Majles approve nationalization
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1951 and month >= 3 and razmara_assassination_seen = 1 and nationalization_approved_majles = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 20
