= 8–15 March 1951

The oil committee recommends the nationalization principle, and the Majles
approves it. The passage is fixed; your choice shapes how the Front explains
the victory and prepares for Senate consideration.

- @nationalization_institution: Protect the institutional record
- @nationalization_public: Consolidate the public mandate

@nationalization_institution
on-arrival: parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 5; constitutional_legitimacy += 3; oil_coalition_support += 3
go-to: post_event

@nationalization_public
on-arrival: public_mandate += 5; organizational_reach += 3; press_capacity += 3
go-to: post_event

@senate_approval
title: The Senate approves nationalization
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: march_action_complete = 1 and nationalization_approved_majles = 1 and nationalization_approved_senate = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 30
on-arrival: nationalization_approved_senate = 1

= 20 March 1951

The Senate approves the nationalization principle. The historical anchor is
complete; the political organization that reaches it reflects eighteen months
of decisions.

- @finish_campaign: Evaluate the campaign

@finish_campaign
on-arrival: campaign_complete = 1
go-to: post_event
